  "limitations": [
    "The uninformative-description list is a conservative keyword rule, not a semantic judgement. It will miss a description that is fluent but wrong ('Search' on a settings button), and that class of error cannot be detected from the view hierarchy at all. Variant E is therefore a lower bound on low-quality labelling.",
    "None of these variants can distinguish a decorative image from a meaningful one, because the view hierarchy does not encode that. The estimates are therefore upper bounds on genuine debt, which is the conservative direction for the paper's claim."
  ]
